:: OC James Intro Quest Part 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You walk into the courtyard, still feeling that uneasy feeling from the cafeteria. <span style="color:Yellow">You can’t shake the feeling you are being watched, the feeling you’ve felt all day. It has made you uneasy and jittery, always looking over your shoulders and jumping at the slightest noise.</span> You just hope that, now that you’re finally on the playground and able to relax, that the feeling will disappear and everything will go back to… <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:Yellow">You feel it again. Stronger than ever! Something is watching you… something is right behind you-!</span> <br>
<br>
You spin around and come face to face with another boy, nervously holding his hands up as he was about to tap your shoulder. <span style="color:Yellow">You both let out a scream of surprise, the boy jumping back and holding his hands up to shield his face.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’m sorry!”</span> He cries as your heart nearly leaps out of your chest. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightGreen">It’s just a kid, another student, a classmate. Whew!</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
      {
            Name: "OC James",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Sorry if I scared you, I was just- I wanted to-”</span> The boy gulps nervously. He seems very uneasy and socially awkward, like he isn’t used to approaching strangers and asking for help. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’m sorry, I’ve been wanting to talk to you all day, but every time I’ve tried, I’ve…”</span> The boy gulps, taking a deep breath. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’m <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span>!”</span> He holds his hand out stiffly, clearly very nervous, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I- I’m in some of your classes, but we’ve never spoken. I- I don’t do good with strangers, but-”</span> <span style="color:Pink">The boy has a stutteriness to his voice, tripping over his own words trying to explain himself. Confused, but curious, you shake his hand and ask if he’s alright.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Yes, f- fine! I- I just wanted to ask you a question.”</span> He takes a deep breath, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“On the boardwalk, there’s this abandoned shop. You know, boarded up and tucked into the corner. No one ever goes there. Do… do you remember going in there?”</span> He looks at you a bit unsure. <span style="color:BlueViolet">His words unlock a memory, like a dream. You do know the shop he’s talking about… did you go inside it?</span> <br>
<br>
You recall seeing the shop, abandoned and empty, but also that it wasn’t? That there was a sign outside the door, a light that welcomed you in? <span style="color:BlueViolet">You see a flash of orange in your brain, but then your head starts to hurt. You remember it like you remember a dream, blurry and confusing. You thought about going in there, you thought you made the decision to go in there, but you don’t actually remember going in. It’s like the thought of that place suddenly… vanished?</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span>’ eyes widen as you explain this, the confusion, the blurry visions, especially when you mention the orange blur. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I knew it!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> leaps forward, an inch away from your face as he grabs your arms. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“The orange, what did it look like? What did the inside of the shop look like?”</span> You nervously step back, feeling a little weirded out. You explain again, you can’t remember anything specific. <span style="color:BlueViolet">It feels like a dream, it probably was a dream… but then how would he know about it? Your head starts to hurt even more.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
      {
            Name: "OC James",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“No, no! I get it! It’s the same with me!”</span> He is smiling now, overjoyed that someone else understands. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I remember the shop, remembering wanting to go in, choosing to go in, but then… Poof!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> makes a motion like his brain exploding. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“It’s like a blur, like it didn’t happen and my head hurts when I think about it, just like you!”</span> You take another step back, starting to feel a little creeped out by this entire situation. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I’ve tried to go back there, go back in the shop, but every time I do, I just… don’t! I can’t explain it. I want to go in, choose to go in, then it’s like I didn’t!”</span> You admit, something about this feels strange. You can’t put your finger on it, <span style="color:Yellow">but the fact that your own memory seems wrong makes you believe that something is wrong.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Exactly! Finally! I’ve tried to talk to my friends about it or my parents, but they just think I’m crazy or making stuff up! But then I saw you, you went inside! Look!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> reaches into his backpack and pulls out a photo… <span style="color:BlueViolet">a photo of you walking into the abandoned shop.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I saw you walk in; I’ve been watching this place and saw you go in. I waited for hours, but you never came out. I thought that something had happened, but then I saw you on the bus! Normal, like nothing happened! And you’re just like me, you can’t remember any of it!”</span> The picture is the straw that breaks the camels back, now you are really freaked out. <span style="color:BlueViolet">You have no memory of walking into this strange shop. Your fear is clear on your face.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“This is perfect! With two of us, we can finally figure out what’s going on!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> looks to you, desperate smile on his face, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You have to help me find out what that place is and why we can’t remember anything! Please, I’m going crazy! I was a few days from asking my parents for a therapist before I saw you walk in.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> falls to his knees, the boy is clearly very desperate for someone to help make sense of this whole thing. <span style="color:Yellow">And you are too. Now that you’ve thought about this shop, seen that picture. Something is definitely going on here.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="Choice">
	<<link "Agree<br>">>
	<<replace"#Choice">>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">Though you may be a little unsure, you agree to help <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> investigate, at least a little. Just until you can understand what’s going on or you get too scared to continue.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">James</span> leaps to his feet, overjoyed at finally having someone to help him piece this all together. He gives you a big, excited hug. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Thank you, thank you, thank you!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He is so giddy he is bouncing,</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright, here’s the plan. Meet me at the Boardwalk Saturday morning when it opens, around 7AM. We’ll head to the shop and figure out what’s in there once and for all. With the two of us, we’ll for sure figure it out!”</span> <br>

